BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vincent\, A Portrait by the Postman Roulin -Theatrical Performance
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTSTAMP:20260922T152512Z
UID:aca5509d45e9d8783d1662015813@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:This intimate and revealing one-man show paints a portrait of 
 the great artist\, Vincent van Gogh\, through the eyes of Vincent’s loya
 l friend\, the Postman Roulin. The postman relays the artist’s amazing p
 ersonal and artistic journey from his native Holland to the South of Franc
 e. You are transported to a café in Auvers\, France in the year 1890. Bef
 ore you are two chairs\, a table\, a baguette in a country basket\, a bott
 le of peasant wine and two glasses. You are asked\, “Would you like to s
 hare my bottle of wine and talk? Sometimes strangers can have the most int
 imate conversations.”\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/vincent-port
 rait-postman-roulin-theatrical-performance
LOCATION:Litchfield Community Center\, 421 Bantam Road\, Litchfield CT\, 0
 6759
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/vincent-portrait-postman-roulin-theatrical-
 performance
END:VEVENT
